
🗺️ Network Topology Addressing Schema

• Router 1 LAN: 192.168.1.0/24 (Gateway: 192.168.1.1)
• Router 2 LAN: 192.168.2.0/24 (Gateway: 192.168.2.1)
• Router 3 LAN: 192.168.3.0/24 (Gateway: 192.168.3.1)
• Serial Link 1 (R1-R2): 10.1.1.0/30 (10.1.1.1 on R1, 10.1.1.2 on R2)
• Serial Link 2 (R2-R3): 10.2.2.0/30 (10.2.2.1 on R2, 10.2.2.2 on R3)

1. Router 1 Configuration Code

text
enable
configure terminal
hostname Router1

! --- CONFIGURE INTERFACES ---
interface GigabitEthernet0/0
 ip address 192.168.1.1 255.255.255.0
 no shutdown
exit

interface Serial0/0/0
 ip address 10.1.1.1 255.255.255.252
 clock rate 64000
 no shutdown
exit

! --- STATIC ROUTE CONFIGURATION ---
! Route to Router 2's LAN via next-hop R2
ip route 192.168.2.0 255.255.255.0 10.1.1.2
! Route to Router 3's LAN via next-hop R2
ip route 192.168.3.0 255.255.255.0 10.1.1.2
! Route to the remote Serial Link between R2 and R3
ip route 10.2.2.0 255.255.255.252 10.1.1.2

end
write memory
Use code with caution.

