! --- STATIC ROUTE CONFIGURATION ---
! Route to Router 2's LAN via next-hop R2
ip route 192.168.2.0 255.255.255.0 10.2.2.1
! Route to Router 1's LAN via next-hop R2
ip route 192.168.1.0 255.255.255.0 10.2.2.1
! Route to the remote Serial Link between R1 and R2
ip route 10.1.1.0 255.255.255.252 10.2.2.1

end
write memory
Use code with caution.

🔍 Verification Commands

Run these commands in the CLI of any router to verify connectivity and route tables:
• show ip route — Verifies that all static routes (marked with a S) are active in the routing table.
• ping 192.168.3.10 — Tests end-to-end connectivity from a PC on LAN 1 to a PC on LAN 3.
• traceroute 192.168.3.10 — Traces each router hop to confirm that paths are traversed properly.
